---
import SiteLayout from '../layouts/SiteLayout.astro';

export const prerender = true;
---

<SiteLayout
	title="Privacy"
	description="Privacy information for Tomorrow-ish."
	canonicalPath="/privacy"
>
	<header class="page-header">
		<p class="section-kicker">The less mysterious fine print</p>
		<h1>Privacy</h1>
		<p>Effective September 11, 2026</p>
	</header>

	<article class="prose-page">
		<p class="prose-page__standfirst">A concise account of how Tomorrow-ish and its service providers handle data.</p>
		<p>
			Tomorrow-ish does not currently offer public accounts, comments, subscriptions, or submission forms. It does
			not currently use a separate audience-analytics service.
		</p>
		<h2>Hosting data</h2>
		<p>
			Our hosting provider may process standard request information needed to deliver and protect the site, such as
			IP address, browser information, requested URL, and request time. Its handling of that information is governed
			by its own terms and policies.
		</p>
		<h2>Advertising</h2>
		<p>
			Tomorrow-ish may use Google AdSense to display and measure advertising. When advertising is enabled, Google
			and its advertising partners may use cookies, local storage, or similar technologies for ad delivery,
			measurement, fraud prevention, and personalization where permitted.
		</p>
		<p>
			Whether personalized advertising is available may depend on your choices and the requirements that apply where
			you live. Where required, visitors will be offered consent or opt-out choices. You can also learn about and
			manage Google's advertising controls through <a href="https://myadcenter.google.com/" rel="noopener noreferrer">My Ad Center</a>.
		</p>
		<h2>External links</h2>
		<p>
			Stories may link to other websites for source or contextual material. Those sites have their own privacy
			practices, which Tomorrow-ish does not control.
		</p>
		<h2>Changes</h2>
		<p>
			This notice will be updated when materially different data collection, analytics, or advertising practices are introduced.
		</p>
		<h2>Questions</h2>
		<p>
			For privacy or data questions, email <a href="mailto:newsgoblin@tomorrow-ish.news">newsgoblin@tomorrow-ish.news</a>
			or visit the <a href="/contact">Contact page</a>.
		</p>
	</article>
</SiteLayout>
